Original commit body from 57705064a56d398616e1d9d478a8e9fc167ee48a:

ADR-0041 §1 under the owner's 2026-10-25 project-frame ruling: tier is the
distance, from the project, of the code a node stands for, and nodes
standing for one package carry one tier. A dependency declaration stands
for the package it names. On dev a sibling declaration was tier 2 in Python
('workspace-internal dependency declaration') and tier 3 'dependency
declaration (external)' in npm, Composer, Cargo and Maven, while the
sibling's own project/package/module node was tier 1 (production-CLI repro,
one two-member workspace per ecosystem).

supply_chain.collect_in_tree_packages replaces the Python-only
collect_workspace_package_names: one walk over the in-tree manifests of
every ecosystem whose manifests both publish a name and declare
dependencies, each compared the way the ecosystem compares names --
pyproject PEP 503, package.json / composer.json exact, Cargo.toml '-' = '_',
pom.xml groupId:artifactId (groupId inherited from <parent>; a declared
${project.groupId} is the declaring module's group). A declaration matches
only a manifest of its own basename (an npm `core` is not the crate
`core`). cli._classify_symbols gives a match the tier the named manifest
classifies to -- the package node's tier by construction, so a package
vendored under third_party/ stays tier 3 -- and the reason
"declares in-tree package <name> (<manifest>)"; two manifests publishing
one name resolve to the lower tier, then the first by path.

sketch._run_analysis's no-map fallback re-implemented classification per
path, tiering every declaration (third-party included) by its manifest's
path, tier 1; it now calls _classify_symbols.

Measured, production `hypergumbo survey`, dev a4546cb836 vs this branch:
  nest     (npm)    172 of 1,379 declarations 3 -> 1; 165 of them are
                    sample/ apps pinning the published @nestjs/* by
                    version (no npm `workspaces` field) -- the package
                    named is still the repo's own, so tier 1 under the
                    ruling; 7 are packages/.
  diesel   (Cargo)  45 of 275, 3 -> 1 (34 from examples/, 11 from
                    workspace crates).
  killbill (Maven)  118 of 683, 3 -> 1.
  poetry   (Python) 0 of 24: its sibling declarations are
                    [tool.poetry.dependencies] tables, which toml_config
                    emits no node for (to be filed as its own item).
  No other node's tier or reason moved; no node set changed; no map has a
  tier-2 node before or after. nest's 4k sketch is byte-identical apart
  from the cache-path footer. Effect beyond the declaration nodes:
  `--max-tier 1` keeps them; tier-weighted centrality weighs them 2x.

Not covered, disclosed in spec §14 §3a: a Cargo dependency renamed with
`package = "..."` (the node carries only its key); go.mod produces no
declaration nodes at all.

